## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native SwiftUI parity of `components/feedback/SessionExpiringModal.tsx` at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/SessionExpiringModal.*`, following the committed `feature-views` architecture (decomposed into surface + Model/Adapter/Projection/Dialog/Chrome + Previews + Tests + AdapterTests + strings — 1592 lines).

**Faithful to the web source + P4 leaf contract:**
- **Open gate** reproduced exactly: dialog presents only when `mode == session && isExpiringSoon && !hasExpired`; otherwise renders nothing (`mode==open`, hard-expired, and pre-resolution all → dormant).
- Live **countdown** (`m:ss`), the capped **unsaved-draft list** with `+N more`, **Stay signed in** (re-poll) / **Sign out now** (re-auth handoff), and scrim-dismiss→stay — all wired through a `SessionExpiringSource` seam (P1/S8). No HTTP/navigation in the view.
- Every mandated state renders & is tested: **loading** (skeleton), **empty** (friendly note), **ready**, **error** (retry — the sanctioned leaf addition), plus the orthogonal **live/stale/offline** axis (chip+banner+one-shot stale auto-refresh) and **refreshing**.
- All web i18n keys in a per-surface table; no English literals (facade-fallback pattern); `view.opened` telemetry (P1/S11); VoiceOver labels, `.isModal` focus trap, reduce-motion.

